    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d802">

                <pb facs="0834" n="732" xml:id="pg732"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">303.1111 M Nielsen, Niels/73: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan (Grew)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-10-26T17:00:00-05:00">October 26, 1933—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>102. Your unnumbered [<hi rendition="#italic">167</hi>,] October 25, 11
                        p.m.<anchor n="44" xml:id="d802-f1"/> Please express to Foreign Office your
                    Government’s appreciation of Japanese official assistance in effecting release
                    of Nielsen; also congratulations on escape of Torihata. Department is
                    instructing Peiping to make similar expression at Peiping and Mukden.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
